  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The District of Columbia recorded $129M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The District recorded 669 awards and the average award size was $193K. Obligations fell 99.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows obligations of $31.6B in FY22, $33.9B in FY23, $36B in FY24, $31.4B in FY25, $33B in FY26, and $129M in FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in FY2027 to date with $40.9M, followed by the General Services Administration with $29.4M and the Department of the Treasury with $21.4M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $19.3M, ERNST & YOUNG LLP received $8.8M, and CENSEO CONSULTING GROUP, INC. received $8.1M. Other Computer Related Services was the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $43.4M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $20.3M and Software Publishers with $9.8M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
